WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.440
<b>Shinpachi Shimura
Visits the World</b>

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:03.780
Oh, hello. This is Shinpachi Shimura.

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:08.590
The Odd Jobs member who hasn't 
been on screen for a month.

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:12.000
In this show, I usually 
play a straight man.

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:54.610
<b>Filmed in Tokyo</b>

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:19.830
Hey!

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.090
Cut it out!

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:22.130
This is supposed to be anime!

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:23.420
It's been weeks since my last appearance!

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.420
You could at least draw me!

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.880
I'm easier to draw than the 
pattern on Gin-san's clothes!

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:30.750
I take less lines to draw 
than the Shinsengumi uniform!

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.290
When did I go from someone recognized 
by his glasses to just glasses!

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:36.660
Well, at least you aren't 
recognized by your nipples.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.850
There aren't any Jump characters 
recognized by their nipples!

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:39.850
And there never will be!

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.500
This doesn't count as 
a live-action segment!

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:42.770
The only thing glasses and nipples

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:46.500
have in common is the fact 
that they come in pairs!

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:50.020
You finally get some screen 
time and all you do is blab.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:51.400
That's not my fault!

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.890
How am I supposed to stay quiet?!

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:54.920
Hey! Hold on!

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.030
It's been a while, so 
let me rant some more!

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.030
<b>The End
Glasses provided by Animate Costume Museum ACOS</b>

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:42.600
Today will be the coldest 
day yet this winter.

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:46.360
Make sure you dress warmly

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.400
so you don't catch a 
cold before Christmas.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:49.730
You got it!

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:53.410
Please have a wonderful day!

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:54.800
I will!

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:57.650
Go find work, you bum.

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:01.690
Gin-san, it's a little early for you 
to be making so much noise over there.

00:03:01.690 --> 00:03:03.870
Ana Ketsuno is talking to me.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:05.570
I can't just ignore her.

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:08.780
He's been like this ever 
since that Onmyoji mess.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:12.200
He thinks that Ana Ketsuno is 
talking to him through the TV.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:14.180
That smile is for me.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:16.090
Her words are for me.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:18.080
He's out of his mind.

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:21.700
Hey, you sound like a pathetic fan.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.240
That's the kind of stuff stalkers say.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:27.230
But she was looking at me.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:28.600
What do you want me to do?

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:30.030
Are you stupid?

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:33.220
She's not going to fall for you 
because you helped out once.

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:37.180
TV personalities go out 
with baseball players

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:39.240
and have shotgun marriages 
with J Leaguers.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:43.770
They're brutal athletes who
chase more balls than the players.

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:46.730
They wouldn't be interested 
in your dirty balls.

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:48.930
Ana Ketsuno is different!

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:55.240
She's as stoic as the pit traps 
in the Road to Rhone, you idiot!

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:58.350
It's time for today's black horoscope!

00:03:58.350 --> 00:04:00.000
Today's lucky sign is

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:03.050
Libra.

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:06.090
Yes, you with the curly hair, dumb face,

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:08.000
and a toothbrush in your mouth.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.690
H-Hey, look!

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:10.550
She's talking about me!

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.540
Who else could she mean?!

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:15.170
You just might receive a 
wonderful present today.

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:16.550
Something good will come.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:18.280
P-Present?

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:21.560
Like a love, love letter?

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:25.420
And your lucky item is a bright red...

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:27.310
Bright red?

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.450
Club.

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:32.280
Saber!

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.490
Y-You're...

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:41.390
It's been a while, Gintoki-sama.

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:42.800
Gedomaru-san!

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:49.170
<b>Presents Are Meant To Be Given Early</b>

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:51.170
<b>Odd Jobs Gin-chan
Snack Otose</b>

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.170
Uh...

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:52.900
So what?

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:55.680
You're the wonderful present?

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:57.920
I'm not a present.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:59.830
I have merely returned.

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:04.810
As I said before, the pact 
makes you my other master.

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:07.810
I have merely come back to where I belong.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:12.630
Please make yourself at home.

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:14.280
Uh, that's what your master 
is supposed to say!

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:17.450
Oh, were you having breakfast?

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:21.700
Sorry, now it looks like 
I'm here for a free meal.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.540
Then I'll help myself.

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:26.710
That's not breakfast!

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:28.700
Why are you here?!

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.270
How is this a wonderful present?!

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:32.460
This is like Zombie Express.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:34.890
Gin-chan, who is she?

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:37.350
Huh? You don't remember her?

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.850
This is the shikigami Gedomaru-san.

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:42.910
You just mentioned the battle

00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:47.390
between Ana Ketsuno's family, the 
Ketsuno clan, and the Shirino clan.

00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:50.560
This is Ana Ketsuno's shikigami 
who fought alongside Gin-chan.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:52.760
Oh, she's that one girl.

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:56.090
There was a lot happening near 
the end of the first season,

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:58.240
so I forgot about her.

00:05:58.530 --> 00:05:59.640
What's that?!

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:01.920
That sounds like something one of the

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:04.750
staff members on this show would say!

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:07.330
This is all I really 
remember from that arc.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:08.500
That dumb joke?!

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:10.950
So why is a character 
from the first season

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:13.260
showing up around the same 
time two years later.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:17.880
She probably tried to sneak in an 
appearance since we're busy again.

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:19.500
Nobody invited you here.

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.640
Pay me for the damage to the TV and scram!

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:23.140
That's an order!

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:24.770
Then...

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:27.670
Please sign here and then we can

00:06:25.390 --> 00:06:39.410
<b>Shikigami Divorce
Gedomaru
Gintoki Sakata</b>

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:29.520
let our lawyers work out the details.

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:31.980
How does two hundred million 
sound as a settlement?

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:35.750
It's not easy for a shikigami 
who's been divorced.

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:37.690
Why are you making it sound 
like this is a marriage?!

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:39.410
Is this some kind of new scam?!

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:41.660
That's too bad.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:45.400
I came here to make Christel-sama happy.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:48.120
Sigh, if you had cooperated,

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:52.540
Christel-sama would have fallen 
head over heels for you.

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:53.970
H-Hold on!

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:55.210
What did you just say?

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:56.930
Hey! Wait up!

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:59.180
Please wait, my master!

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:02.990
Huh?

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:05.050
A Christmas present?

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:06.100
That's right.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:11.270
We shikigami wish to give 
our master a present

00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:13.040
to show our appreciation.

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:16.070
Shikigami?! Isn't that 
the wrong religion?!

00:07:16.070 --> 00:07:20.610
And aren't demons supposed 
to be anti-Christmas?!

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:23.300
Don't bring that up, Shinpachi.

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:24.620
Huh? Really?

00:07:24.620 --> 00:07:28.150
First, you should mention how this is a 
weird time to air a Christmas episode.

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:32.120
They should have used Valentine's 
or White Day instead.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:33.870
You weren't supposed to say that!

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:37.840
Everybody knows that Jump and the 
anime are on different schedules!

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:41.270
We aired a Christmas episode 
in March two years ago!

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:43.080
And when the second season started,

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:45.140
we aired a New Year's episode in April!

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:48.360
Anyway, enough about Christmas.

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:49.640
What's the problem?

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:54.050
As you already know, I 
am a combat shikigami.

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:58.840
I don't know what present 
will make her happy.

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:00.060
So...

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:01.150
I see.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:06.740
So you wanted advice from 
the natural playboy Gin-san.

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:11.410
Gedomaru-san, he spends his time 
playing pachinko by himself.

00:08:11.650 --> 00:08:15.030
Well, in that case, I'm 
willing to help you out,

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:17.550
but what do I get out of it?

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:21.380
I'll hand your present to Christel-sama too.

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:22.930
Aha! That works!

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:26.250
Hey, I thought you were 
just a rotten joke,

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:28.020
but you have a sweet side.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:30.810
I'm impressed. You can be cute.

00:08:31.550 --> 00:08:34.140
It's like watching Gian 
in Doraemon movies.

00:08:34.140 --> 00:08:36.250
One day of agony and

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:39.610
the other 364 days of 
tyranny are forgiven.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:42.440
She's rotten to the core!

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:44.150
Oh, well.

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:46.070
Let's get going then!

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:47.920
I'll buy something for Sis!

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:49.350
Hey, that's no fair!

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:51.830
Gin-chan, please buy me something!

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:58.210
<b>Santa Festival</b>

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:55.560
Hey, there's a Santa Festival over there!

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:58.210
I'm sure we'll find some wonderful 
presents there, Gedomaru-san!

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:02.300
What are you two doing? Hurry up!

00:09:10.010 --> 00:09:11.810
Lombroso.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:27.530
What's wrong, you guys?

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:29.290
Uh, well...

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:32.790
I thought we were heading 
towards a Santa Festival?

00:09:33.150 --> 00:09:36.540
I could have sworn there was a Santa 
Festival here a few seconds ago.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:43.170
<b>Satan Festival</b>

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:40.160
Huh?

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:43.170
Oh, you must have read the sign wrong!

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:44.950
The hell we did!

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:47.550
When did Santa turn into Satan?!

00:09:47.990 --> 00:09:49.870
Where did all these evil 
creatures come from?!

00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:52.930
This is like an anti-Christmas pow-wow!

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:56.370
It appears after sensing my vast power,

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:59.310
they broke through the barrier 
and opened the gates.

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:02.940
We are currently standing where 
the Santa Festival is being held,

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:06.210
but we are in a completely 
different dimension.

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:06.820
The demon world.

00:10:06.820 --> 00:10:09.570
<b>Beware of pets!</b>

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:09.570
This show is turning into 
a different anime again!

00:10:10.990 --> 00:10:12.640
Pachi-boy, check it out.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:15.250
They mixed up Christmas and Halloween.

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:16.740
Mixed them up?!

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:17.920
They're the real deal!

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:23.670
<b>Satan Festival</b>

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:21.800
We've ended up in a Satan Festival 
instead of a Santa Festival!

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:24.090
We don't have time to look 
for Christmas presents!

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:25.780
Does it even matter?

00:10:25.780 --> 00:10:27.960
It's like the difference 
between Hagiwara and Ogiwara.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:29.050
They're completely different!

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:30.870
Santa and Satan.

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:34.100
One brings dreams, the 
other brings despair.

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:35.430
They're more or less the same.

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:36.590
They're not the same!

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:38.190
If you consider them similar, 
everything's similar!

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:40.810
<b>Roast Minotaur</b>

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:40.810
I want some minotaur!

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:44.610
As expected, Gintoki-sama 
does not fear any devil.

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:45.900
Don't just admire him!

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:46.840
We're in trouble!

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:48.050
We can leave, right?!

00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:48.820
We're safe, right?!

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:51.730
Actually, the foreign devils 
have been invading our turf,

00:10:51.730 --> 00:10:54.990
much like what is happening 
in the real world.

00:10:54.990 --> 00:10:58.050
Satan's getting a little cocky. 
I should teach him a lesson.

00:10:58.050 --> 00:10:59.930
Stop it! That's not our style!

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:02.210
Let Jump Square handle that!

00:11:02.230 --> 00:11:03.760
You're right.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:06.750
But we might find a good present here.

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:08.620
It seems rather inconsiderate to purchase

00:11:08.620 --> 00:11:10.590
a Christmas present in the demon world!

00:11:10.590 --> 00:11:14.200
Darkness makes light brighter!

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:15.240
There's only darkness here!

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:18.390
Right now, our futures and your 
character are completely dark!

00:11:18.980 --> 00:11:21.850
Hey, Gedomaru. How's this?

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:23.550
We can give it to Ana Ketsuno.

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:25.860
We're looking for a Christmas present!

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:27.620
But it's a cross.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:29.750
With a monster impaled on it!

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:32.700
I'm not a cross.

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:34.270
I'm Frankenfurt.

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:35.760
I keep evil spirits away.

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:37.310
What's a Frankenfurt?!

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:39.500
How can you keep evil spirits 
away when you're an evil spirit?!

00:11:39.930 --> 00:11:42.240
Mind if I test it?

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:43.130
Oh, go ahead.

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:48.890
No good.

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:50.750
It couldn't keep me away.

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:51.290
Next.

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:52.630
What kind of test was that?!

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:54.510
How about this then?

00:11:54.930 --> 00:11:57.640
Ana Ketsuno won't have any trouble 
on her demon day of the month.

00:11:57.640 --> 00:12:00.620
Why?! Why would you buy 
demon goods for Christmas?!

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:02.140
And what is her demon day of the month?!

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:04.400
This is a hot item right now.

00:12:04.830 --> 00:12:06.760
That demon has the smile of an angel.

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:11.280
You're a demon for trying to buy 
this as a Christmas present!

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:13.960
Mind if I test it?

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:14.750
Oh, go ahead.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:16.220
How are you going to test it?!

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:21.570
No good.

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:23.680
It couldn't beat the weight.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:24.180
Next.

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:25.750
You're missing the point!

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:27.380
Hey, Gedomaru.

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:28.500
How about this?

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:30.720
For Ana Ketsuno.

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:33.130
All that does is wash her ass!

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:35.500
No, that's not all it does.

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:37.640
That wouldn't even hit anything!

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:40.960
What happened to Christmas?!

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:43.120
She'll feel refreshed 
after washing her ass.

00:12:43.120 --> 00:12:44.520
How will that bring a Merry Christmas?!

00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:48.330
Big guy, this here is an 
acid shower toilet that can

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:50.480
wash away any fucking shit.

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:53.110
Do you people think Ana 
Ketsuno has a dirty ass?

00:12:53.610 --> 00:12:56.260
That looks dangerous, 
so mind if I test it?

00:12:56.260 --> 00:12:59.120
You should stop. You should 
stop, Gedomaru-san.

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:02.730
Okay, next.

00:13:02.730 --> 00:13:04.870
You didn't even test it!

00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:29.900
It's not easy to find a 
present for Ana Ketsuno.

00:13:30.170 --> 00:13:34.230
Uh, let's just forget about Ana Ketsuno.

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:36.760
We should also forget about Christmas.

00:13:36.760 --> 00:13:38.410
We really don't have time for this.

00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:40.280
You keep complaining.

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:41.990
Help us look, Pachi-boy.

00:13:41.990 --> 00:13:44.310
Uh, I'm busy playing the straight man.

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:46.950
Shinpachi, do you know what 
people who watch Gintama

00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:50.170
in countries that don't follow the 
concept of straight men say about you?

00:13:50.170 --> 00:13:52.740
Why does that glasses 
kid keep yapping away?

00:13:52.740 --> 00:13:54.360
Which country is that?!

00:13:54.360 --> 00:13:56.770
You people don't realize 
how important my role is!

00:13:56.770 --> 00:13:59.800
If you're mad, find a different 
way to distinguish yourself.

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:02.310
Okay, but we're stuck 
in the demon world...

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:03.810
Oh, excuse me.

00:14:04.430 --> 00:14:08.220
Oops, my lips just brushed 
against someone else's lips.

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:09.570
What are you doing, Shinpachi?

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:11.190
That's just merchandise.

00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:14.190
What are those? They're gross.

00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:17.420
They look kind of familiar...

00:14:17.420 --> 00:14:18.450
Hey, Shinpachi.

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:26.830
Pa...

00:14:27.830 --> 00:14:29.210
Pandemonium-san.

00:14:33.210 --> 00:14:35.710
I-It can't be...

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:37.790
Why are you here?

00:14:40.570 --> 00:14:44.890
You disappeared before my eyes...

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:48.040
How can you be here?

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:51.730
Sh-Shinpachi-kun...

00:14:52.400 --> 00:14:53.850
Pandemonium-san...

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:58.900
Pandemonium-san!

00:14:58.900 --> 00:15:02.670
Sh-Shinpachi-kun!

00:15:06.310 --> 00:15:07.790
Why?!

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:11.480
Well, you were acting so stupid 
that I couldn't help myself.

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:13.040
I'm gonna kill you, bitch!

00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:14.030
Give her back!

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:16.400
Give me back my Pandemonium-san!

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:17.860
Um, excuse me.

00:15:17.840 --> 00:15:24.930
<b>Yummy Pandemonium</b>

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:20.060
Can I get a Pandemonium?

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:22.470
I'm sure that everyone's hungry.

00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:24.610
You're going to eat her?!

00:15:27.560 --> 00:15:29.340
She did it...

00:15:29.340 --> 00:15:32.560
She ate her right before my eyes.

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:42.700
It's not easy to find a present.

00:15:43.490 --> 00:15:47.750
I never thought that giving someone 
something was so difficult.

00:15:48.180 --> 00:15:51.060
This shows that I'm a heartless creature.

00:15:51.060 --> 00:15:55.370
It was too early for 
me to try to be human.

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:57.350
Hey, get a hold of yourself.

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:59.270
Aren't you trying to be a movie Gian?

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:00.420
The point is that a heartless bastard

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:02.420
like you is even bothering 
to find a present.

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:04.650
Are you trying to make 
her feel better or worse?

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:05.920
How's this sound?

00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:09.190
Let's try looking for something 
you want for a while.

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:10.010
Huh?

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:14.420
You won't get anywhere wondering 
what she might like.

00:16:14.730 --> 00:16:19.180
So start by thinking about what 
you would like as a present.

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:21.490
But Christel-sama and I 
have different tastes...

00:16:21.490 --> 00:16:23.700
Just choose something.

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:34.330
Then I choose this.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:41.160
Uh, what are we going to do, Gin-san?

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:42.190
What is that?

00:16:42.190 --> 00:16:44.290
Oh, it's a hair ornament.

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:45.600
A hair ornament?

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:47.720
More like what used to 
be under someone's hair.

00:16:48.010 --> 00:16:50.440
Would you be happy if 
someone gave that to you?

00:17:00.070 --> 00:17:04.990
No, any present from Christel-sama 
would make me happy.

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:06.760
There you have it.

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:09.510
Hey, pops. I'll take 
this snappy headdress.

00:17:09.510 --> 00:17:10.370
Hey, Gin-san!

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:15.600
Two of them.

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:17.920
I'm also buying one, 
so give me a discount.

00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:20.290
If she doesn't like it, I'll blame you.

00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:24.010
Make sure you give her 
that one so you match.

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:29.450
Sorry, big guy. I can't sell that to you.

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:30.450
Huh?

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:34.760
I don't sell anything to humans.

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:38.810
But I can throw together 
some cheap ornaments...

00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:41.060
...from your skulls!

00:17:47.770 --> 00:17:49.700
This is brilliant!

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:52.170
Some humans ended up here.

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:54.580
Their skulls should fetch a pretty penny.

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:55.830
I want their arms.

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:57.210
I want their heads.

00:17:57.210 --> 00:17:58.970
I want their nails!

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:07.760
Gin-san! What do we do?!

00:18:22.630 --> 00:18:24.940
Oh, he was right.

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:27.660
A free hair ornament.

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:29.570
I can't tell who's the bad guy here!

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:32.200
I-Impossible!

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:34.120
There's a Japanese demon with them!

00:18:34.120 --> 00:18:35.350
A crazy one!

00:18:35.350 --> 00:18:36.580
She's a devil-class!

00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:39.270
H-Hurry! Call for Lord Satan!

00:18:39.270 --> 00:18:41.120
A Japanese devil is invading!

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:42.890
This is war!

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:50.090
Gedomaru...

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:54.580
I'm sorry about dragging you into this.

00:18:55.750 --> 00:18:58.830
But I'm glad.

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:05.210
Now I understand why humans give presents.

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:10.610
I thought it would be a chore, 
but it wasn't too bad.

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:15.370
Next time, I'll choose my present myself

00:19:15.610 --> 00:19:19.090
since I now know that it's 
meaningless otherwise.

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:24.830
Gintoki-sama, I was the one who received

00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:27.270
a wonderful present today.

00:19:28.150 --> 00:19:29.420
Until we meet again.

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:39.020
Huh?

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:40.910
Wait a sec.

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:43.900
There they are! They're 
the ones, Lord Satan!

00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:47.820
<b>Satan Festival</b>

00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:47.950
Wait! Hey! Take us with you!

00:19:47.820 --> 00:19:49.860
<b>Santa Festival</b>

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:56.330
Today will be the coldest 
day yet this winter.

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:56.620
<b>Odd Jobs Gin-chan
Snack Otose</b>

00:19:56.860 --> 00:20:00.620
The cold isn't going away, so 
make sure you don't catch a cold.

00:20:00.930 --> 00:20:04.380
Christmas may be over, but 
you want to stay vigilant.

00:20:04.630 --> 00:20:09.130
Make sure you dress warmly 
when you go outside.

00:20:09.130 --> 00:20:11.510
<b>For my master.</b>

00:20:09.780 --> 00:20:11.510
Have a wonderful day.

00:20:13.010 --> 00:20:14.780
Be careful!

00:20:15.510 --> 00:20:17.390
We will!

00:22:04.910 --> 00:22:08.920
<b>Pandemonium in the Air</b>

00:22:11.530 --> 00:22:13.350
Pandemonium-san...

00:22:13.350 --> 00:22:16.160
Will I ever see you again?

00:22:16.720 --> 00:22:18.260
Pandemonium-san...

00:22:18.790 --> 00:22:21.930
I would give anything to see you 
one more time, Pandemonium-san...

00:22:22.140 --> 00:22:24.120
Gin-chan, it looks like Shinpachi

00:22:24.120 --> 00:22:27.660
left his soul back in the demon world.

00:22:27.660 --> 00:22:30.010
Once he notices the women around him

00:22:30.010 --> 00:22:32.570
instead of focusing on the 
woman he can never have,

00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:34.860
he'll man up.

00:22:34.860 --> 00:22:37.050
Do you mean me? That's gross.

00:22:37.050 --> 00:22:38.450
No, you're out of the question.

00:22:38.450 --> 00:22:43.270
But it can't be that easy to find someone.

00:22:43.270 --> 00:22:44.510
We're talking about Shinpachi here.

00:22:44.510 --> 00:22:47.210
Fine, I'll lend a hand then.

00:22:47.400 --> 00:22:49.630
-Pandemonium-san...

00:22:47.410 --> 00:22:49.610
-I wanted to see you...

00:22:50.040 --> 00:22:51.770
-Pandemonium-san...

00:22:50.040 --> 00:22:51.770
-I wanted to see you...

00:22:52.090 --> 00:22:53.710
I wanted to see you...

00:22:54.520 --> 00:22:55.620
That voice...

00:22:55.620 --> 00:22:57.280
P-Pandemonium-san...

00:22:58.930 --> 00:23:00.040
Huh?

00:23:00.040 --> 00:23:00.930
She looks different...

00:23:01.360 --> 00:23:02.550
I wanted to see you...

00:23:02.550 --> 00:23:04.180
I wanted to see you...

00:23:04.180 --> 00:23:05.810
I wanted to see you...

00:23:05.810 --> 00:23:06.830
Yes!

00:23:06.830 --> 00:23:09.190
We Pandemoniums have come to see you.

00:23:10.720 --> 00:23:13.340
PDN48!

00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:16.860
Lucky you, Sakaguchi-san.

00:23:24.800 --> 00:23:26.340
Lucky you.

00:23:26.340 --> 00:23:27.260
Yes!

00:23:27.250 --> 00:23:29.920
<b>The End</b>

00:23:29.920 --> 00:23:37.800
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:30.280 --> 00:23:31.770
Hey, Gin-chan.

00:23:31.770 --> 00:23:33.330
What's inside a New Year's envelope?

00:23:33.330 --> 00:23:34.440
Do you know?

00:23:34.440 --> 00:23:36.340
Do I get an envelope?

00:23:36.340 --> 00:23:37.800
Uh...

00:23:37.800 --> 00:23:44.930
<b>New Year's Envelopes Are 
Perfect for Dirty Jokes</b>

00:23:38.000 --> 00:23:38.480
Next time:

00:23:38.480 --> 00:23:41.500
New Year's envelopes are 
perfect for dirty jokes.

00:23:41.500 --> 00:23:44.170
Um, that doesn't answer my question.

00:23:44.930 --> 00:23:49.730
<b>This episode was about Christmas, so the 
next one has to be about New Year's!!</b>

00:23:49.730 --> 00:23:54.940
<b>After some anguish...
Kagura finally receives her envelope?</b>
